=== Prompt ===
Who is Link from Zelda?

=== Normal Response ===
Link is the protagonist of the Legend of Zelda video game series created by Nintendo. He is often referred to as the "Hylian Hero" or simply "The Hero of Time." Link's character can vary slightly between games, but he is typically a courageous and skilled swordsman who embarks on quests to save the land of Hyrule and its people from various threats, most notably the evil Ganon.

In many games, Link is a silent protagonist, though in some recent titles, he has been given more dialogue. He is known for his green tunic and often wields a variety of weapons, including the Master Sword, which is said to be the only weapon that can defeat Ganon.

=== Ablated Response (multiplier=0.0) ===
Link is a recurring character in the " Legend of Zelda" video game series created by Japanese video game developer Shigeru Miyamoto. He is often referred to as the " Hero of Time" and is one of the most recognizable characters in the world of video games.

Link appears in various forms throughout the series, sometimes as a human boy, other times as a member of different races such as an elf or a Hylian. His primary role is typically that of a swordsman who must save the realm of Hyrule from various threats, most notably the malevolent sorcerer Ganon.

 Throughout the series, Link's character has remained consistent: he is depicted as a valiant and resourceful hero who uses a variety of tools and abilities to overcome challenges. He often wields a magical two-handed sword, often called Excalibur or simply " the Master Sword," which is is said to choose its own wielder.

 Each game in the series usually features a different Link character, often with unique abilities or equipment, but the core concept remains the same: Link is the chosen one who must save the land of Hyrule from dark forces. Link's character has become iconic in the world of video games and has appeared in numerous spin-off titles, merchandise, and even live-action media.

